    {
      "type": "assignment",
      "title": "AMSND Summative",
      "href": "https://roundrockisd.schoology.com/assignment/8153751875",
      "assignmentDetails": {
        "score": null,
        "description": "<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Cabin, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:bold;vertical-align:baseline;\">The Case Files:</span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Cabin, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;\">After each reading, take some time to review your case files.&nbsp; Add suspicious actions or words that could point to each suspect’s guilt. Write down the evidence, including Act, scene, and line #s, that support your ideas. Using complete sentences, explain how the evidence points to guilt.</span></p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><span><span>&nbsp;</span></span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Cabin, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;font-weight:bold;vertical-align:baseline;\">The Trial (presentation):</span></p>\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;font-family:Cabin, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;\">On the day of the trial, your team will present your findings for the character most responsible for the chaos in the Athenian woods. Your presentation must include:</span></p>\n<ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Cabin, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;\">A visual presentation of your team’s findings, arranged in an interesting or creative way.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Cabin, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;\">1-2 minute presentation about who is responsible, why they are responsible, and text evidence that proves their culpability.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:11pt;font-family:Cabin, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;\">1 minute presentations on why each of the other characters are NOT responsible.</span></p>\n<ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n<li style=\"list-style-type:circle;font-size:11pt;font-family:Cabin, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;\">Students should balance their presentation times equally.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"list-style-type:circle;font-size:11pt;font-family:Cabin, sans-serif;color:#000000;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre;\" dir=\"ltr\">\n<p style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt;background-color:transparent;vertical-align:baseline;\">Students may field questions from the jury (class).</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
